 "provenance": {
  "breakers": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the wiring diagram 810-04-1596-WYE rev A draws two banks of three two-pole breakers (\"MONITORED OCPs\"), each bank feeding 18 outlets. Its drops alternate three colours along a bank, so each outlet is on the breaker its position leaves after three, 1 2 3 1 2 3 from the bank's cord side; the data sheet lists \"Alternating Phase Outlet Technology\". Which breaker takes which line is not labelled and is not stated."
  },
  "capability": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - the PRO4X data sheet's family table gives Smart input current monitoring and branch circuit protection and neither outlet control nor per outlet power monitoring, and the SKU page prints Outlet Monitoring None and Branch Monitoring Current (A). So `metering-scope: branch` and `outlet-switching: false`, and no outlet declares a state vocabulary."
  },
  "chassis": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - 1778.2 long and 55.9 wide. The side view's body is 63.5 deep; the outlets stand about 14.4 beyond it, which makes the 77.9 callout. THAT READING IS FROM THE SIDE VIEW'S GEOMETRY, not a label."
  },
  "ends": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - the end views show a plate with the cord entry at one end and two screws at the other. The cord end's entry frame is drawn from its end view; no view shows the cord itself, so none is drawn."
  },
  "front": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the plan view. From the cord end: an end plate with the cord entry, the label panel, a three-breaker module, 18 outlets in groups of 3, 6, 6 and 3, the controller panel, a second three-breaker module and 18 more outlets in the same groups. Outlet positions are the centres of each outlet's lamp window; the C13 pitch is 21.18 and the HDOT Cx pitch 26.69, measured from the paths and not dimensioned. THE STANDARD C13 RECESS IS 22.0 ALONG, WIDER THAN THE 21.18 PITCH, so each C13 triplet is spaced at 22.0 about its drawn middle, up to 0.8 mm off the drawn centres."
  },
  "input": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "drawing and datasheet - the wiring diagram titles the unit 3PH WYE and draws a plug with L1, L2, L3, NEUT and GND. The SKU page for C4S36RA-GPBD2FE1 prints Input Plug Type \"230/400 32A & 240/415V Wye 30A IEC 60309 3P+N+G 6Hr\", 415 V, 30 A (24 A rated), 17.3 kW and Input Cord Location Bottom/Angled; the drawing serves five SKUs and the other four print other plugs, so only this SKU's is stated. The fixed cord is one part at the cord end, drawn as the end view shows its entry frame (29.2 across), and every outlet is fed by it. The cord's length and gauge and the plug's face are in no held document (gaps: cord-and-plug)."
  },
  "method": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "THE FACES ARE THE 4G16A'S, READ FROM THE SAME DRAWING. The maker's outline drawing 810-03-1596-00 is titled C4x36RA-GPBD2FE1 and this family's SKU page lists it, the wiring diagram 810-04-1596-WYE and a stencil and a 3D model of the same title, so one outline serves the four families. No held photograph or drawing is specific to this family: the one photograph is a single generic image (the same file on all four family pages), so the controller panel is taken to be the 4G16A's (gaps: family-faces). FIGURES FROM THE MAKER'S VECTOR DRAWING. Server Technology outline drawing 810-03-1596-00 rev A (sheet 1, 11-Dec-2021) draws the strip lying down, cord end left, with a plan view, a rear view above it, a side view and an end view, and a detail A of the outlets. Its views are paths, so positions were read off the PDF's geometry at 0.42483 pt/mm, the scale that puts the 1778.2 overall on the strip; the 68.4, 88.4, 422.4 and 1555.8 button dimensions land within 0.9 mm at it. The library draws the PDU STANDING, cord end down, so a position along the drawing becomes 1778.2 minus that, and a position across becomes x. The STEP model in the maker's archive was not read: no reader for it is held."
  },
  "mount": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "`rack-side`: the strip stands beside a rack's upright on mounting buttons at the back. The outline dimensions eleven positions along the back; the maker's mounting data sheet says a kit is two buttons, and a PDU wider than 45 mm takes two kits. Which positions carry buttons on this SKU is not stated, so the pair 1555.8 apart, the dimensioned one, is drawn (gaps: button-positions)."
  },
  "numbering": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - read from a render, not text extraction. Detail A prints 36, 35, 34 at the cord end and 19 beside the controller; the far bank prints 18 beside the controller and 1 at the far end. Outlet 1 is drawn at the far end from the cord. The per-SKU data sheets (page 2) for the four SKUs of this family ending BD2FE1 print \"Outlet #1 opposite the power input\", the numbering drawn. The data sheet for the SKU ending BD2EE1 prints \"Outlet #1 at the power input\", the opposite end. That SKU is not listed here."
  },
  "outlets": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - the PRO4X data sheet says HDOT Cx is a hybrid of the IEC C13 and C19 and HDOT C13 is its C13. The twelve HDOT C13 are drawn as std/c13-outlet@1 (the retention feature is not drawn). The HDOT Cx is servertech/hdot-cx-outlet@1, an estimate: no dimensioned outlet drawing is held."
  },
  "rear": {
